     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It&#39;s not identical, but does this help? (See &quot;Per-session objects&quot;)<div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/scoping.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/scoping.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393889506000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1VutFBMX1ufvfGH3fNfYZm\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/scoping.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>If not, let&#39;s talk about what your overall app is trying to do. Concepts from traditional web frameworks often don&#39;t map well to Shiny because we don&#39;t use an HTTP request/response model, but rather reactive-programming message passing over a websocket; even if you can do it &quot;their&quot; way in Shiny, there&#39;s often a better way to do it with reactivity.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sat, Apr 23, 2016 at 7:45 PM Yoav Gal &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yoav...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:16.9px\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding-right:15px;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"text-align:center;min-width:46px\"><span style=\"margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:20px;display:block;color:rgb(106,115,124)\"><br></span><a title=\"This question does not show any research effort; it is unclear or not useful\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:10px;margin-left:auto;font-size:1px;color:rgb(0,119,204);overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-position:0px -220px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" rel=\"nofollow\">down vote</a><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/36818728/is-there-a-r-shiny-equivalent-for-net-session-variables#\" title=\"Click to mark as favorite question (click again to undo)\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:2px;margin-left:auto;font-size:1px;color:rgb(0,119,204);overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-position:0px -120px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/36818728/is-there-a-r-shiny-equivalent-for-net-session-variables%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393889506000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1CWqv5stFwQZUUzxMAg--u\">favorite</a><div><span style=\"color:rgb(106,115,124)\"></span></div></div></td><td style=\"vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;font-size:15px;width:660px;word-wrap:break-word;line-height:1.3\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">I am looking for something similar in a Shiny app, that would be similar to .NET&#39;s <a href=\"https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms178581.aspx\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,89,153)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms178581.aspx&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393889506000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n2jZ6B_KaUZLnSCmbJGQ4\">session variables</a>.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">What I&#39;m trying to do is to store different variables at the session level, to be used across different functions. Is there a way to do that?</p></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/d945e2